---
title: "Chris McCann — Field Notes"
description: "Consciousness research. Leadership. The gap between what leaders do and what they're carrying when they do it. Newsletter, assessment, book."
canonicalUrl: "https://chrismccann.co"
permalink: /index.html
---
{%- extends "base.njk" -%}

{% block header %}
  <header class="fade-in">
    <h1>Chris McCann</h1>
    <div class="subhead">Fifteen years leading sales teams.<br>Still figuring it out.</div>
    <div style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      <p style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--gray); letter-spacing: 0.03em; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Consciousness. Leadership. The gap between them. Two pieces a month.</p>
      <form id="homepageSubscribe" style="display: inline-flex; gap: 0; max-width: 380px; width: 100%;">
        <input type="email" id="homeEmail" required placeholder="Your email" aria-label="Email address"
          style="flex: 1; padding: 10px 14px; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.85rem; border: 1px solid var(--light-gray); border-right: none; background: #fff; color: var(--black); outline: none; min-width: 0;">
        <button type="submit" id="homeSubBtn"
          style="padding: 10px 20px; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; background: var(--black); color: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--black); cursor: pointer; white-space: nowrap; transition: opacity 0.2s;">Subscribe</button>
      </form>
      <div id="homeSubSuccess" style="display: none; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--accent); margin-top: 0.5rem;">You're in. Check your inbox.</div>
      <div id="homeSubError" style="display: none; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.85rem; color: #c0392b; margin-top: 0.5rem;">Something went wrong. Try again.</div>
      <script>
      document.getElementById('homepageSubscribe').addEventListener('submit', async function(e) {
        e.preventDefault();
        const email = document.getElementById('homeEmail').value.trim();
        const btn = document.getElementById('homeSubBtn');
        if (!email) return;
        btn.textContent = '...';
        btn.disabled = true;
        try {
          const res = await fetch('/.netlify/functions/subscribe', {
            method: 'POST',
            headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
            body: JSON.stringify({ email: email })
          });
          if (res.ok) {
            document.getElementById('homepageSubscribe').style.display = 'none';
            document.getElementById('homeSubSuccess').style.display = 'block';
          } else {
            document.getElementById('homeSubError').style.display = 'block';
            btn.textContent = 'Subscribe';
            btn.disabled = false;
          }
        } catch (err) {
          document.getElementById('homeSubError').style.display = 'block';
          btn.textContent = 'Subscribe';
          btn.disabled = false;
        }
      });
      </script>
    </div>
  </header>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="fade-in">
      <p>In my early twenties I managed Hooters restaurants. Fifteen years later I was leading go-to-market for SaaS companies. Same job underneath: read the room, set the tone, try not to be the reason people dread Monday stand-ups.</p>
      <p>I got good at the measurable stuff. Forecast calls, SKOs, quarterly reviews. What I didn't track was the energy. One Tuesday a rep closed the biggest deal in company history and the room felt dead. Numbers were right. Everything else was off. I realized the thing that was off was me.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="fade-in">
      <p>That sent me somewhere I wasn't expecting. I started noticing what I carried into rooms before anyone spoke. What my body already knew that my calendar didn't. The gap between the version of me running the meeting and whatever was underneath it.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="fade-in">
      <p>The deeper I looked at what creates that field, the more I had to look at myself.</p>
      <p>Co-authoring a book with <a class="inline-link" href="https://drwarter.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Dr. Carlos Warter</a> (Park Street Press, spring 2027) on the nature of the field itself — what it is, how to sense it, and what it means for how humans organize, decide, and evolve.</p>
      <p>Field Notes is where I work through the questions before the book has answers for them.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="divider fade-in"><span class="colophon"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect x="6" y="0" width="8.49" height="8.49" rx="1" transform="rotate(45 6 0)" fill="none" stroke="#ccc" stroke-width="1"/></svg></span></div>

    <section class="article-list fade-in" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      <h2 class="section-label">Recent Writing</h2>
      <div id="recent-posts"></div>
      <p style="margin-top: 1rem;"><a class="inline-link" href="/field-notes/">All Field Notes &rarr;</a></p>
    </section>
    <script>
      fetch('/posts.json')
        .then(r => r.json())
        .then(posts => {
          const container = document.getElementById('recent-posts');
          posts.slice(0, 3).forEach(post => {
            const div = document.createElement('div');
            div.className = 'article-item';
            div.innerHTML = '<h3><a href="' + post.url + '">' + post.title + '</a></h3><p class="article-excerpt">' + post.excerpt + '</p>';
            container.appendChild(div);
          });
        });
    </script>
  </main>

  <div class="fade-in" style="margin: 3rem 0; padding: 2rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--light-gray); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--light-gray); text-align: center;">
    <h2 style="font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">THE FIELD ASSESSMENT</h2>
    <p style="font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--black); line-height: 1.7; max-width: 480px; margin: 0 auto 1.5rem;">Twenty-four questions. Five minutes. Two parts. What you're carrying into the room. What the room is doing with it.</p>
    <a class="cta-btn-outline" href="/field-assessment/">TAKE THE ASSESSMENT</a>
  </div>
{% endblock %}

{% block subscribe %}{% endblock %}

{% block head %}
  <script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Person",
    "name": "Chris McCann",
    "url": "https://chrismccann.co",
    "jobTitle": "Writer",
    "description": "Fifteen years leading sales teams. Still figuring it out.",
    "image": "https://chrismccann.co/images/og-default.png",
    "sameAs": [
      "https://www.linkedin.com/in/chrismccannco/"
    ],
    "email": "chris@chrismccann.co"
  }
  </script>
{% endblock %}
